+On Linux, when the supervisor switches to an explicit numeric `run_as_user`,
+it clears supplementary groups before changing UID. The child keeps the
+selected primary GID but does not inherit the supervisor's supplementary groups
+or resolve group memberships from a matching named account. If clearing groups
+fails, the child does not start. This does not reset groups for an
+already-unprivileged process that keeps its current UID.
